{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs","id":987485,"title":"How would you sell the Forsaken Koolaid to Cubs?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-14T16:14:19-07:00","id":987485,"title":"How would you sell the Forsaken Koolaid to Cubs?","content":"So i running this cubs game in werewolf. Pc started as freshly change werewolf and im running their first hunt. The pcs are normal people (a lawyer, a teacher and a bouncer) who a month ago transformed and have no idea of the setting (so no tribes yet) and i had planned a sort of &quot;moot&quot; for the players to get introduced but i kind got myself into a problem.<br /> <br /> As i was thinking on how the elder werewolf would explain the &quot;setting&quot; to them i ran into the problem that well being a forsaken kind of sucks. Not from a player perspective but from a character perspective. <b><u>So how do you sell the duty of the forsaken to newly changed cubs?</u></b><br /> <br /> Because as i was thinking it, all i would could think is<br /> <br /> &quot;So hey, you guys are werewolves and you have to leave your human lives aside and help us do this spiritual thankless duty. Spirits will hate you for it, other bad werewolf will hate you while coming to kick you out and then take your stuff because you doing it. And from time to time we also will come and kick you out and take your stuff because you arent doing it as good as we do&quot;<br /> <br /> I kind of write myself into a corner here also because in my game im running the pure as the sabbat, in the sense that they represent the werewolf who schew their duty and live &quot;free&quot; because one of the players has a trigger with the &quot;hate group that comes and burn you and take your family and reprogram you&quot; interpretation of them. So i kind struggling how to sell the setting to the characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T16:24:43-07:00","id":987486,"title":"","content":"Are you playing first edition?<br /> <br /> Because in second your duty is the hunt. If you neglect it, you weaken and lose control and fall into Kuruth at the drop of a hat. And you don't have to leave your human lives behind. You can if you want but it's not necessary. This is why there's a Lodge of the Shield, and the Pack has packs formed from a band, a software programming company, a fire house and a hospital. They didn't turn into werewolves and decide, 'Well I suppose I should become a police officer now.' You do have to recognize, or at least you should, that you aren't human anymore, however. And spirits may not like you, but many will at least respect you, providing you've earned it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-14-2016, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T18:05:40-07:00","id":987521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987486#post987486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you playing first edition?<br /> <br /> Because in second your duty is the hunt. If you neglect it, you weaken and lose control and fall into Kuruth at the drop of a hat. And you don't have to leave your human lives behind. You can if you want but it's not necessary. This is why there's a Lodge of the Shield, and the Pack has packs formed from a band, a software programming company, a fire house and a hospital. They didn't turn into werewolves and decide, 'Well I suppose I should become a police officer now.' You do have to recognize, or at least you should, that you aren't human anymore, however. And spirits may not like you, but many will at least respect you, providing you've earned it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am using the denver sourcebook so its kind of 1st. I mean i am using the 2ed rules but the theme is gonna be insolationist packs vs protectorate.<br /> <br /> Well yes there is those example but those are of packs that all share the same job. This is a pack with a colegue proffesor, a lawyer and a bar bouncer. Get in hunts regularly is gonna interfere with their jobs one way or another as their jobs are their anchors (the thing that they almost can have of they surrender to the human lives per the description of the core)<br /> <br /> They dont have tribes yet and i will be trying to get then to hunt one of each to choose their favorite prey and thus their tribe.<br /> <br /> But struggling on how to sell the character the forsaken faction. Even if i were to change their duty to hunting for huntings sake or else degeneration. The pure have easier prey, and the spirit already respect them.<br /> <br /> I guess my main question is. The pure have a great selling pitch. What would be a great forsaken selling pitch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T18:53:02-07:00","id":987533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987521#post987521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yes there is those example but those are of packs that all share the same job. This is a pack with a colegue proffesor, a lawyer and a bar bouncer. Get in hunts regularly is gonna interfere with their jobs one way or another as their jobs are their anchors (the thing that they almost can have of they surrender to the human lives per the description of the core)</div> </div> </div> </div>They can interfere but they shouldn't too much. Lawyers, professors and bouncers have time off too. During pack creation they had opportunity to make wolf-blooded and human members who could support their lives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They dont have tribes yet and i will be trying to get then to hunt one of each to choose their favorite prey and thus their tribe. </div> </div> </div>You might not want to portray it as 'favorite prey.' As that sounds like, 'Yeah we love killing these.' Instead they believe they are the most dangerous prey, and thus need to be hunted. But the tribes have other aspects to them than just their sacred prey. Storm Lords are about strength, fortitude, perseverance, the Ithaeur are about wisdom and knowledge and secrets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But struggling on how to sell the character the forsaken faction. Even if i were to change their duty to hunting for huntings sake or else degeneration. The pure have easier prey, and the spirit already respect them.<br /> <br /> I guess my main question is. The pure have a great selling pitch. What would be a great forsaken selling pitch? </div> </div> </div>The duty of the werewolf is to hunt. It's not for hunting's sake. It's because they're part 'spirit of the hunt.' They aren't human. They are a living, breathing Predator. If they do not perform the Sacred Hunt, they will make Breaking Points towards the Flesh. They will lose Essence. They will not be able to change willingly, to heal Lethal wounds, to use their powers. They will be triggered by passive triggers beyond their control, simply their moon being in the sky even if they're inside and asleep. This is not changing anything, it's how the game works. Your pack gets to choose what they hunt, what they think is the most dangerous, what they think is worth it, what they think deserves it, and what they think is so wrong it needs to be eradicated.<br /> <br /> I like the Pure. The spirits don't respect them any more than the Forsaken. They like using them. They like taking advantage of them not giving a damn the way the Forsaken do, but they don't respect them unless they've earned it the same as the Forsaken. And the Pure are the ones who have to leave their humanity behind. Two of the tribes, at least. The Predator Kings cannot use things made by humans. The Fire-Touched cannot let lies stand. There's a reason they live in the wilderness and the Hisil, respectively.<br /> <br /> Between that and 'Lets just burn that Renown off you,' I don't know why you get the idea the Pure have a great selling pitch. Their methods of conversion include torture and brainwashing. I could understand if you said your characters were backwoods survivalists or hellfire and brimstone preachers but are they really the type to fall for the Pure? Some people want to destroy the world as it is, and that fits for the Pure, but the path of the Forsaken doesn't involve destroying humanity and civilization as we know it.<br /> <br /> You shouldn't have a hard time with it. A character explains the history of the Uratha. Urfarah, Mother Luna, Pangaea. He weakened, was overthrown, the Uratha were exiled from their home, cursed with madness as a result. Eventually the Uratha earned back the grace of the spirits, the Firstborn totems and Luna. She marks them with Renown so that spirits will know she watches over them. The Firstborn give them a path so they can become what they're truly meant to be. She gave them the Oath of the Moon, so they can know how to find Harmony and self-control over their ever-shifting natures.<br /> <br /> The tribes should be open enough to fit them. If for some reason they don't like the tribes, they can remain a ghost wolf. The introduction wouldn't really have to even mention the Pure, though mentioning that some wolves want to tear it all down or serve twisted alien gods probably isn't out of the ordinary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-14-2016, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T19:26:48-07:00","id":987550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987521#post987521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess my main question is. The pure have a great selling pitch. What would be a great forsaken selling pitch?</div> </div> </div> </div>How the flying <i>fuck</i> do the Pure have a &quot;great selling pitch&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T19:35:33-07:00","id":987555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987550#post987550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How the flying <i>fuck</i> do the Pure have a &quot;great selling pitch&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hey, kid, you wanna be a spiritual orphan who can't touch silver, serves greedy spirits, and forms tight bonds around bigotry, zealotry, and making your own clothes? What if I told you that to join, we spend all night cutting off your skin over and over? Still no? Whaddya want, a signing bonus?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T19:37:11-07:00","id":987557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987533#post987533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between that and 'Lets just burn that Renown off you,' I don't know why you get the idea the Pure have a great selling pitch. Their methods of conversion include torture and brainwashing. I could understand if you said your characters were backwoods survivalists or hellfire and brimstone preachers but are they really the type to fall for the Pure? Some people want to destroy the world as it is, and that fits for the Pure, but the path of the Forsaken doesn't involve destroying humanity and civilization as we know it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because as i said, i cant use much of the torture and brainwashing because<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs#post987485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of write myself into a corner here also because in my game im running the pure as the sabbat, in the sense that they represent the werewolf who schew their duty and live &quot;free&quot; because one of the players has a trigger with the &quot;hate group that comes and burn you and take your family and reprogram you&quot; interpretation of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So i am using the angle of the pure less as the &quot;we dragged you and reprogram you&quot; and more &quot;we tempt you and offer you &quot;freedom&quot; without telling you the tag price&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987533#post987533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tribes should be open enough to fit them. If for some reason they don't like the tribes, they can remain a ghost wolf. The introduction wouldn't really have to even mention the Pure, though mentioning that some wolves want to tear it all down or serve twisted alien gods probably isn't out of the ordinary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont have that much problem with the tribes themselves. One of the players already has the idea of becoming a storm lord. but on how to sell them the forsaken &quot;society&quot; without it being a ticking bomb to a &quot;half the party is gonna join the &quot;sabbat&quot;&quot; situation<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987550#post987550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How the flying <i>fuck</i> do the Pure have a &quot;great selling pitch&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhmm because they do have one? Im not saying OOC they are right or that their selling pitch is true. But that, in their book they said that the pure (fire touched mostly) would put their best face forward when recruiting. They will sell the to-be-convert on all the power, &quot;righteousness&quot;, &quot;absolution&quot; and &quot;freedom&quot; they gain by joining them without mentioning the fine print (the inhumane totem requirements, the fuck up society, etc). So i am asking for a similar selling pitch for a forsaken to give newly change forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T19:47:02-07:00","id":987560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987557#post987557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So i am using the angle of the pure less as the &quot;we dragged you and reprogram you&quot; and more &quot;we tempt you and offer you &quot;freedom&quot; without telling you the tag price&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose in that case all you have to do is have a Forsaken point out the price. But if you're getting rid of the werewolf limitations just for the Pure, and getting rid of the torture, then you've certainly made them a more tempting thing to join. Even the Sabbat had to deal with frenzy and in-fighting and backstabbing.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised you even bothered introducing the Pure like that. There's already a group that lives in 'freedom' from the Tribes and Luna, the ghost wolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dont have that much problem with the tribes themselves. One of the players already has the idea of becoming a storm lord. but on how to sell them the forsaken &quot;society&quot; without it being a ticking bomb to a &quot;half the party is gonna join the &quot;sabbat&quot;&quot; situation </div> </div> </div>Even with that trigger warning, you can have them at war with the Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T19:58:28-07:00","id":987566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987560#post987560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose in that case all you have to do is have a Forsaken point out the price. But if you're getting rid of the werewolf limitations just for the Pure</div> </div> </div> </div>Limitations?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987560#post987560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and getting rid of the torture, then you've certainly made them a more tempting thing to join. Even the Sabbat had to deal with frenzy and in-fighting and backstabbing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the firetouched too have infighting, rage and just a shitty society but is not something the pc will see at first glance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987560#post987560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised you even bothered introducing the Pure like that. There's already a group that lives in 'freedom' from the Tribes and Luna, the ghost wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the game was already set to start. And i got a new player, who is from the previous game and when i sold them the pitch of the game, she was all onboard with that but she has had some heavy experience with torture and reprogramming. I am not talking about somehow who uses the term &quot;triggered&quot; casually, i mean real life &quot;i still have night terrors and psychological problems about this&quot;. <br /> <br /> So she asked me if we could avoid the subject, as is the reason she havent being able play Apocalypse neither. So i read the pure book and found that angle and though &quot;sure I can still run denver with this.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987560#post987560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with that trigger warning, you can have them at war with the Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes they are at war. They just dont take prisioners. Killing/fighting is fine to her, is the idea of RPing brainwash/torture that is an issue.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T20:08:10-07:00","id":987571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987566#post987566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Limitations?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wolf Must Hunt. Without the Sacred Hunt you hit Breaking Points and lose Essence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well the firetouched too have infighting, rage and just a shitty society but is not something the pc will see at first glance. </div> </div> </div>But they can't lie about it. Someone would just have to ask or bring it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T20:18:24-07:00","id":987579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987571#post987571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wolf Must Hunt. Without the Sacred Hunt you hit Breaking Points and lose Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do have a sacred hunt<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Preview;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Fire-Touched hunt those who dishonor and disrespect the Shadow. Anyone who harms or tyrannizes a spirit without provocation, or who attempts to seal away the Hisil, such as by thickening the Gauntlet or closing a locus, gains the zealous hatred of the Izidakh. This may include unwitting humans who disrespect icons or idols representing spirits. Disrespect to Luna and her servants doesn\u2019t earn the Fire-Touched\u2019s enmity, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way the angle of &quot;freedom&quot; works between 1st and 2nd is that the firetouched promise is one in which you hunt those who disrespect the shadows and in exchange you get gift/approval from the spirits. You dont have to keep your territory in line, just set the humans that are offlimits to the spirits and in exchange you protect them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987571#post987571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they can't lie about it. Someone would just have to ask or bring it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but even the book recognizes lies by omision and incomplete truths are valid. I mean &quot;do you guys fight each other?&quot; can be answered &quot;truthfully&quot; with &quot;Disagree happen from time to time but we are united, in our purity&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 10-14-2016, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T20:41:00-07:00","id":987584,"title":"","content":"The Forsaken sales pitch is that they can teach you to cope with your whole turning into a 400 pound snarling death beast a few nights out of every month problem. That happens because your Harmony is borked, and the Forsaken can teach you to balance your Harmony. The Wolf Must Hunt, and the Tribes can show you the best ways to turn that need to hunt to good use - better you hunt the Werewolves that can't control their rage, or renegade spirits, or Claimed, or the Hosts, or hell, even bad people than to hunt who or what ever happens to be closest to you when you lose control. And the Forsaken can give you the means, the know-how, and the opportunity to channel your Primal Urge safely. Sure, the Pure aren't bound by Luna's laws, but those laws are there for a reason. Breaking them pushes you further from your spirit nature and puts you at greater risk of losing control. Sure, you can counteract that by abandoning civilization and running wild as a King of Predators, or by abandoning the world of flesh to Touch the Fire of the spirit world, or by abandoning your humanity in pursuit bleaching your Claws the Ivory of racial purity. But those paths all come with great sacrifice and great risk, not to mention being morally dubious. It's order and discipline versus freedom and chaos. Do you join those who know how to carefully moderate their dual natures, or those who throw themeselves headlong towards alternating extremes with reckless abandon? Do you maintain a careful balance or risk fluctuating wildly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T20:47:23-07:00","id":987588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987584#post987584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Forsaken sales pitch is that they can teach you to cope with your whole turning into a 400 pound snarling death beast a few nights out of every month problem. That happens because your Harmony is borked, and the Forsaken can teach you to balance your Harmony. The Wolf Must Hunt, and the Tribes can show you the best ways to turn that need to hunt to good use - better you hunt the Werewolves that can't control their rage, or renegade spirits, or Claimed, or the Hosts, or hell, even bad people than to hunt who or what ever happens to be closest to you when you lose control. And the Forsaken can give you the means, the know-how, and the opportunity to channel your Primal Urge safely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this, so far i put them on a token hunt. I dont remember where (i think it might be 1st ed) there was rite/custom to make a simulacrum hunt for a spirit, i use that as the first game to break them in on the new mechanics (they never playerd NWoD) so maybe put them to hunt a predator in the university campus (one of the characters works there) that target racial minorities (the specialty of the lawyer) as to give them a common human enemy. <br /> <br /> And break a little of the setting by making other young members of the establish pack help them with them hunt so they see what that help get them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T21:24:54-07:00","id":987594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987486#post987486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you playing first edition?<br /> <br /> Because in second your duty is the hunt. If you neglect it, you weaken and lose control and fall into Kuruth at the drop of a hat. And you don't have to leave your human lives behind. You can if you want but it's not necessary. This is why there's a Lodge of the Shield, and the Pack has packs formed from a band, a software programming company, a fire house and a hospital. They didn't turn into werewolves and decide, 'Well I suppose I should become a police officer now.' You do have to recognize, or at least you should, that you aren't human anymore, however. And spirits may not like you, but many will at least respect you, providing you've earned it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, Forsaken 2e isn't Apocalypse with the Curse preventing the protagonists from the most basic human contact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T23:54:07-07:00","id":987648,"title":"","content":"It's kind of a minor problem with the setting IMO.<br /> <br /> The setting assumes the Pure and the Forsaken are the majority (specifically, the Pure). Both factions sound bad from a purely human mindset, IMO especially if the human in question is very 'neutral' and &quot;live and let live&quot; or just &quot;undecided.&quot;<br /> <br /> So why not just go Ghost Wolf? I feel like the real reason a werewolf wouldn't go Ghost Wolf is that they'd feel lonely and most Ghost Wolves are disorganized and not necessarily present in their area. So they'd be alone... really alone! It would tear at their heart everyday. They'd be confused. They'd be vulnerable to the things that go bump in the night, which they feel the need to hunt. Werewolf lore is ALL about the pack, even the nonsense Twilight movies. So alone... But the two factions? They would introduce you to the world of wolves. Sort of a tutorial and potentially the place where you'd meet your pack or be pointed in the right direction.<br /> <br /> The other reason is that since the Pure are more numerous (esp in 1st edition) they are very forceful about recruitment. The Fire Touched straight up won't take no for an answer and would attempt brainwashing. A Predator King interested in your strength would kick the shit out of you, schoolyard bully style, complete with torture. Ivory Claws are just kind of assholes, but if you're related to them or their extended pack in anyway, they wouldn't let you go Ghost Wolf easily.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: I just read the part about one of your players not wanting to be exposed neither to brainwashing nor to torture. Unfortunately, you've kind of written yourself into a corner in the conflict with such limitations. I feel like all 3 Pure tribes would be willing to do it to a potential recruit. I'd have the Ivory Claws be the main Pure tribe of the area, as they'd be less prone to such issues.<br /> <br /> The problem then is that your characters are all already cubs, technically Ghost Wolves, at the moment. They already have their pack and know each other? So loneliness is hard to play up.<br /> <br /> The easiest way to sell them on the Forsaken is to portray the Pure as villains. Or if they are willing to give the Pure a chance, then let them see that they are evilish (and hopefully your players are more neutral/good-aligned).<br /> <br /> However, much like the current election where both candidates try to sell themselves as &quot;I may be bad, but at least I'm not the other guy,&quot; fear doesn't inspire as much as actual inspiration. In addition to making the Pure stereotypically evil, you could make some of the Forsaken in the area stereotypically good. For example, maybe the local Pure don't care about the local Beshuli infestation and are even rumored to allow them to fester, as they want to combine both worlds and bring back Pangaea. Cue the local Hunters in Darkness or Iron Masters, who valiantly sacrifice their lives to protect their turf or to protect their local humans and community.<br /> <br /> Or maybe have the local Pure be incompetent, while the Forsaken are competent?<br /> <br /> If you want less stereotypes and want to have more neutral leaning Pure, show off some of that infighting you mentioned. Hard to do without physicality because of your sensitive player, but maybe you can just show off the Forsaken as being more 'together.' Maybe the local Forsaken are less alpha-oriented or are even democratic. Maybe there's a local Ghost Wolf with red brands who used to be Pure and severely regrets becoming Pure.<br /> <br /> 2nd Edition is *<b>much*</b> less about being spirit police. If that aspect of the game bothers you, you could have the local Forsaken be heretics who let the occasional spirit trespass as long as they have proven themselves valuable allies and don't harm the local human ecosystem. Basically give more incentive to be Forsaken, even if it means abandoning some of the usual rules. It also sets up a fun encounter much deeper into your campaign if out-of-region Forsaken visit and cause a fuss.<br /> <br /> Since being Forsaken *or* Pure can suck hugely, you could let them remain Ghost Wolves. Try to play up the feeling of loneliness, maybe their first totem acquisition fails as the spirit judges them to be fake wolves since they're not Pure or Forsaken. Play up that they don't really know what they're doing. Drag them into wars they're not fighting (local spirits or hosts come to kill them, confusing them for another pack) Give the Cahalith dreams of them all dying alone, confused, hunted by all manner of things but notably hunted by both the Pure and even the Forsaken (foreboding!) Give them reasons to join up, although no need to railroad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11106,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","user":"Captain Shoe","date":". 10-15-2016, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","name":"Captain Shoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T03:59:07-07:00","id":987700,"title":"","content":"Do you want to join a bunch of nutjobs who hate humans and everything they create, a bunch of nutjobs who make the craziest of religious fundamentalists look sane, or what are basically furry Nazis? If not, the Pure tribes are probably not for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T04:45:30-07:00","id":987704,"title":"","content":"Being able to fulfil your instincts without having to be a psycho sounds like a good enough pitch to me....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T05:21:46-07:00","id":987708,"title":"","content":"For me, Forsaken are all about embracing Uratha role 'humane way' - they want to go with moderation for Flesh &amp; Spirit, they respect humans and spirits, and try to bring out order to those worlds. More, Forsaken are <b>devoted</b> to humans ( <i>The Uratha Shall Cleave To The Human </i>) treating them as real family. Pure would happily made slaves from humanity, just before making world crazy hell it was at Pangea times - mentioning how humans were hunted then by <i>everything, </i>living in fear about tomorrow, should easily stroke the cords in players that Forsaken are much more rational in the end.<br /> <br /> Just point that Forsaken try to be 'humans but werewolves', while Pure try to be as much inhuman as they can get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T05:47:32-07:00","id":987711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987557#post987557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So i am asking for a similar selling pitch for a forsaken to give newly change forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div> How about going with brutal honesty? &quot;Hey guys, you do realize that the Pure Tribes are a bunch of racists, religious zealots, and violent luddites? Being a werewolf isn't easy, and we can help you learn to deal with that, and not fuck up the world and everyone else around you. Find a bit of balance in your life. Give you the tools you need to thrive. Think about it, look around, and give us a call when you're ready.&quot;<br /> <br /> No matter how you paint it, the Pure are still going to have Harmony shoved strongly in the low-Spirit range, and all that implies, and it will be noticable. Their Tribal bans still push for racial purity, flipping out over &quot;blasphemous&quot; words (ie someone disagreeing with the Fire Tongues), and rejection of man made conviences like modern medicine for your human friends/family. The spirit allies are going to be obviously pushing for their agenda without regards to the sanctity of life of anyone or anything else. These pitches are going to fall apart with any amount of objective observation. The Forsaken really don't need to do anything other than offer an alternative and hope the newbies aren't willing to make excuses for bad behavior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 10-15-2016, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T07:16:45-07:00","id":987731,"title":"","content":"&quot;Also, the Pure hate smartphones, at the end of the day.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T08:08:51-07:00","id":987752,"title":"","content":"I would say the Forsaken (and the Pure) seems to know more about what they're doing than Ghost Wolves (aside from some well established lodges). They share knowledge about not only, how to deal with turning into a big, furry killing machine, but also how to deal with the various horrors that werewolves starting running into like spirits, hosts and other werewolves. Running around negotiating with spirits without learning their rules is going to lead to all manner of nasty consequences that you would never imagine. And if your friend was killed and puppetted by a creepy rat monster, how do you know what to do when it bursts into a thousand little rats, assuming you got that far?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T09:57:30-07:00","id":987803,"title":"","content":"My two cents:<br /> <br /> For the Pure side, just make the characters meet reallity by happenstance. If your point is to guarantee a No Pure pack, without asking this OoC, so just make something happen in the game, not planned by the Pure converters, to show how the Pure are Big B Bad Guys, whyle the Forsaken are the Rude But Cool Guys. It'll probably take care of all your problems, but...<br /> <br /> If you have a problem with the selling pitch of the duty of a Forsaken, just don't sell it at all. Make the Forsaken explain things to the characters, including the problems that the spirits are going to cause just because they're f*cking alien beings from another world. Taking care of the Shadow isn't about Sacred Duty most of the time, is just sheer necessity. Then let the PCs join the tribes just because it is good to have someone to back you up.<br /> <br /> You don't have to attach that to the duty at all. Make the NPC Forsaken the kind of people who firmly believe in their religion, but don't require the same from others, not even to join the club. The &quot;duty&quot; will come naturally to your PCs just because they will have to solve problems. Play local and personal until they are convinced that they need to do this shit, not because Duty or boring Prozelytizers command, but because the shit have to be done, or they'll face uncomfortable consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T11:17:33-07:00","id":987848,"title":"","content":"If you'll read above, you'll note that LokiRavenSpeak is not using the Pure as written, and has taken the hate group, torture and brain-washing out of the picture and instead established them as a 'freedom' group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T11:29:06-07:00","id":987851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987848#post987848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you'll read above, you'll note that LokiRavenSpeak is not using the Pure as written, and has taken the hate group, torture and brain-washing out of the picture and instead established them as a 'freedom' group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay but first of all is not, &quot;not using them as written&quot; the pure sourcebook list what i am doing a a valid interpretation and is supported on their sourcebook. Meaning the whole free from duty angle.<br /> <br /> Second, the group is good with violence and the hate group. Just not the forcefull conversion angle. In a nutshell is this, if they can convince you to join with their perceived perks the good, if not they off you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:33:01-07:00","id":987890,"title":"","content":"And we advise on 'free' angle of Pure - if Forsaken would not do their fights, spirits would over rule world of Flesh under Pure government. Humans would become slaves to monsters. And then Pure would want to recreate Pangea as the hell hole it was to humanity.<br /> <br /> If PCs hold dearly human families and packs, they <i>will</i> oppose Pure agenda on this, even without supremacist takes on Pure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T14:08:36-07:00","id":987929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987803#post987803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My two cents:<br /> <br /> For the Pure side, just make the characters meet reallity by happenstance. If your point is to guarantee a No Pure pack, without asking this OoC, so just make something happen in the game, not planned by the Pure converters, to show how the Pure are Big B Bad Guys, whyle the Forsaken are the Rude But Cool Guys. It'll probably take care of all your problems, but...<br /> <br /> If you have a problem with the selling pitch of the duty of a Forsaken, just don't sell it at all. Make the Forsaken explain things to the characters, including the problems that the spirits are going to cause just because they're f*cking alien beings from another world. Taking care of the Shadow isn't about Sacred Duty most of the time, is just sheer necessity. Then let the PCs join the tribes just because it is good to have someone to back you up.<br /> <br /> You don't have to attach that to the duty at all. Make the NPC Forsaken the kind of people who firmly believe in their religion, but don't require the same from others, not even to join the club. The &quot;duty&quot; will come naturally to your PCs just because they will have to solve problems. Play local and personal until they are convinced that they need to do this shit, not because Duty or boring Prozelytizers command, but because the shit have to be done, or they'll face uncomfortable consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yeah i will probably do that. Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T18:04:09-07:00","id":988027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/987485-how-would-you-sell-the-forsaken-koolaid-to-cubs?p=987550#post987550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How the flying <i>fuck</i> do the Pure have a &quot;great selling pitch&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally am drawn to the Predator kings a great deal. Ya'll should read operation werewolf if you get a moment, good stuff btb. The pitch for the pure is different per tribe as they all seem to have their own goals within the over arching goal. The Predator Kings are pure alpha and nothing less. Pretty good pitch imo.<br /> <br /> Also, you sell the koolade like the christians do. You teach them your peoples truth and nothing else, save that everything else is a heresy. Its what the moon has been doing forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T05:08:19-07:00","id":988209,"title":"","content":"My take is that, when an established Forsaken character is trying to 'sell' a new werewolf on becoming Forsaken (rather than Ghost Wolf - the 'don't join those maniacs' pitch vs the Pure is fairly easy), they talk about what being Forsaken actually offers as opposed to going it alone. There's not much need to talk about the myths, the legends and all the deep history stuff. The new werewolf has bigger immediate issues - issues that the Forsaken Tribes can give answers and solutions to. 'Well, there was this mighty spirit called Father Wolf who did XYZ, and the Moon herself said ABC' is nonsense stuff for the werewolf who is still in his or her early days of the new existence. It doesn't matter much. What matters is the friendly offer of knowledge and advice about the new state of being, the offer of the Tribal support network, and so on. The rest comes later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}